g the Sum Rule","answers":[{"id":62298065,"created":"2026-10-15T19:29:39.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15826,"number":1,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 7:29 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":71167,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":371,"text":"<p>$\\displaystyle{\\int 5 - x^3 \\, \\textrm{d}x = }$</p>\n","choice1":"$ 5x - \\dfrac{x^4}{4}+ C$","choice2":"$5x - x^4 + C$","choice3":"$ 5 - \\dfrac{x^3}{4}+ C$","choice4":"$ 5x^2 - \\dfrac{x^4}{2}+ C$","choice5":"$ 5x + \\dfrac{2x^4}{3}+ C$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n\\int 5 - x^3\\, \\textrm d x       & =  5\\int 1 \\, \\textrm d x -  \\int x^3 \\,  \\textrm d x\\\\[5pt]\n                                            & =  5\\int x^{0} \\, \\textrm d x - \\int x^3 \\,  \\textrm d x\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t& =5\\left(\\dfrac {x^{0+1}}{0+1}\\right) -\\dfrac{x^{3+1}}{3+1} + \n                                                 C\\\\[5pt]\n                                             & = 5x - \\dfrac{x^4}{4}+ C\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":3769,"name":"The Sum Rule for Indefinite Integrals"},"example":{"id":371,"title":"Computing an Integral Using the Sum Rule"},"group":{"id":16578,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14249144,"answer":{"id":62298065,"cread":"2026-10-15T19:29:39.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15826},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62298077,"created":"2026-10-15T19:29:56.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12785,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 7:29 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":71169,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":371,"text":"<p>Find the integral of $\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^3}} + 4.$</p>\n","choice1":"$-\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}  + 4x + C$","choice2":"$-\\sqrt{x} + 4x + C$","choice3":"$-\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}  + 3x + C$","choice4":"$\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^3}}  - 4x + C$","choice5":"$-\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}  - x + C$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\eqalign{\n\\displaystyle \\int\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^3}} + 4 \\, \\textrm{d}x&= \\int \\dfrac{1}{x^{3/2}} \\, \\textrm{d}x + 4\\int 1 \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\\[5pt]\n\n& = \\int x^{-3/2} \\textrm{d}x + 4 \\int x^0 \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt]\n\n&= \\dfrac{x^{-3/2+1}}{\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{2}+1\\right)} + 4\\left(\\dfrac{x^{0+1}}{0+1}\\right)+C\\\\[5pt]\n\n\n&= -2 \\cdot x^{-1/2} +  4x + C\\\\[5pt]\n\n\n&= -\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}  + 4x + C\n\n}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":3769,"name":"The Sum Rule for Indefinite Integrals"},"example":{"id":371,"title":"Computing an Integral Using the Sum Rule"},"group":{"id":97332,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14249144,"answer":{"id":62298077,"cread":"2026-10-15T19:29:56.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":12785},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":372,"number":2,"title":"Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules","answers":[{"id":62298091,"created":"2026-10-15T19:30:23.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13540,"number":3,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 7:30 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":49059,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":372,"text":"<p>$\\displaystyle{\\int \\dfrac{x^5+7}{x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x = }$</p>\n","choice1":"$\\dfrac{x^4}{4} - \\dfrac 7 x + C$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{x^3}{4} - \\dfrac 7 x + C$","choice3":"$\\dfrac{x^6}{6} - \\dfrac 7 {x^3} + C$","choice4":"$\\dfrac{x^3}{3} - \\dfrac 7 {x^2} + C$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{x^3}{3} - \\dfrac 7 {x} + C$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n      \\int \\dfrac{x^5+7}{x^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x &= \\int \\left( x^{3} +\\dfrac{7}{x^2}  \\right)\\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[3pt]\n \t\t\t\t\t\t    &= \\int x^{3} \\, \\textrm{d}x + \\int 7x^{-2} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[3pt]\n                                                   &= \\int x^{3} \\, \\textrm{d}x + 7\\int x^{-2} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[3pt]\n \t\t\t\t\t\t   & = \\left(\\dfrac{x^{4}}{4}\\right) + 7 \\left(\\dfrac{x^{-1}}{-1}\\right) + C \\\\[3pt] \n \t\t\t\t\t\t   &= \\dfrac{x^4}{4} - \\dfrac 7 x + C. \n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":3769,"name":"The Sum Rule for Indefinite Integrals"},"example":{"id":372,"title":"Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"},"group":{"id":51870,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14249144,"answer":{"id":62298091,"cread":"2026-10-15T19:30:23.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13540},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62298102,"created":"2026-10-15T19:30:42.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14947,"number":4,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 7:30 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":49063,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":372,"text":"<p>Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int \\sqrt x(2+x)  \\, \\textrm{d}x }.$</p>\n","choice1":"$ \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{x^5}}{5} + \\dfrac{ 4\\sqrt{x^3} }{3} + C $","choice2":"$  \\dfrac{5\\sqrt{x^5}}{2} + 3\\sqrt{x^3}+ C$","choice3":"$  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{x^5}}{5} + \\dfrac{ 2\\sqrt{x^3} }{3} + C $","choice4":"$  \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{x^3}}{3} - \\dfrac{ 4 }{\\sqrt{x}} + C$","choice5":"$  \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{x^3}}{3} + \\dfrac{ 4 }{\\sqrt{x}} + C $","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get</p>\n<p>\\begin{align}\n \t\t\\int \\sqrt x(2+x) \\textrm{d}x &= \\int x^{1/2}(2+x) \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt]\n                                                 &=\\int \\left( 2x^{1/2} +x^{3/2} \\right) \\textrm{d}x\\\\[5pt]\n                                                 & = 2\\int x^{1/2}\\textrm{d}x +  \\int x^{3/2} \\textrm{d}x\\\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t & = 2\\left(\\dfrac{2x^{3/2}}{3} \\right) + \\left(\\dfrac{2x^{5/2}}{5} \\right) + C \\\\[5pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t & = \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{x^5}}{5} + \\dfrac{ 4\\sqrt{x^3} }{3} + C. \n \n\\end{align}</p>\n","topic":{"id":3769,"name":"The Sum Rule for Indefinite Integrals"},"example":{"id":372,"title":"Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"},"group":{"id":55680,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14249144,"answer":{"id":62298102,"cread":"2026-10-15T19:30:42.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14947},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":373,"number":3,"title":"Integrating Sums of Power Functions","answers":[{"id":62298137,"created":"2026-10-15T19:31:07.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15841,"number":5,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 7:31 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:16","question":{"id":113850,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":373,"text":"<p>Find the antiderivative of \n$\\displaystyle \\sqrt[5]{x^4} - x + \\dfrac{2}{x^4}.$</p>\n","choice1":" $ \\dfrac  {5\\sqrt[5]{x^9}}{9} - \\dfrac{x^2} 2 -\\dfrac{2}{3x^3} +C$","choice2":"  $ \\dfrac  {5\\sqrt[5]{x^4}}{4} - \\dfrac{1}{2x} -\\dfrac{2}{3x^6} +C$","choice3":"  $ \\dfrac  {9}{5\\sqrt[5]{x^9}} - \\dfrac{2} x -\\dfrac{6}{x^3} +C$","choice4":"   $ \\dfrac  {4}{\\sqrt[5]{x^4}} - \\dfrac{2}{x^2} -\\dfrac{6}{x^4} +C$","choice5":"  $ \\sqrt[5]{x^9} - 2x^2 -\\dfrac{2}{3x^3} +C$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\eqalign{\n\\int \\left(\\sqrt[5]{x^4} - x + \\dfrac{2}{x^4}\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x\n& =   \\int x^{4/5} \\, \\textrm{d}x - \\int x \\, \\textrm{d}x +2 \\int x^{-4} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\\[5pt]\n\n&= \\dfrac{x^{4/5+1}}{\\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}+1\\right)} - \\dfrac{x^{1+1}}{(1+1)}+2 \\cdot \\dfrac{x^{-4+1}}{(-4+1)}  +C\\\\[5pt]\n\n&= \\dfrac{x^{9/5}}{\\left(\\dfrac{9}{5}\\right)} - \\dfrac{x^{2}}{2}+2 \\cdot \\dfrac{x^{-3}}{(-3)} +C\\\\[5pt]\n\n&= \\dfrac  {5\\sqrt[5]{x^9}}{9} - \\dfrac{x^2} 2 -\\dfrac{2}{3x^3} +C.\n\n\n}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":3769,"name":"The Sum Rule for Indefinite Integrals"},"example":{"id":373,"title":"Integrating Sums of Power Functions"},"group":{"id":55691,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14249144,"answer":{"id":62298137,"cread":"2026-10-15T19:31:07.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":15841},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62298158,"created":"2026-10-15T19:31:27.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14103,"number":6,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 7:31 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":113848,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":373,"text":"<p>Find the antiderivative of \n$\\displaystyle \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x^4}} + x^3 - \\dfrac{1}{x^2}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$-\\dfrac  {3}{\\sqrt[3]{x}} + \\dfrac{x^4}{4} + \\dfrac{1}{x} +C$","choice2":" $-\\dfrac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{x^4}} + \\dfrac{x^2}{2} + \\dfrac{1}{x} +C$","choice3":" $\\dfrac{\\sqrt{x^3}}{3} + 4x^4 + \\dfrac{x}{2} +C$","choice4":" $-\\dfrac  {3}{\\sqrt[3]{x}} + \\dfrac{x^2}{4} + \\dfrac{1}{x^3} +C$","choice5":" $\\sqrt[3]{x}+ \\dfrac{x^4}{4} - \\dfrac{x}{4} +C$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\eqalign{\n\\int \\left(\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x^4}} + x^3 - \\dfrac{1}{x^2}\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x\n& =   \\int x^{-4/3} \\, \\textrm{d}x + \\int x^{3} \\, \\textrm{d}x - \\int x^{-2} \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\\[5pt]\n\n&=  \\dfrac{x^{-4/3+1}}{\\left(-\\dfrac{4}3+1\\right)} +\\dfrac{x^{3+1}}{\\left(3+1\\right)} -\\dfrac{x^{-2+1}}{\\left(-2+1\\right)} +C\\\\[5pt]\n\n&= \\dfrac{x^{-1/3}}{\\left(-\\dfrac{1}3\\right)} +\\dfrac{x^{4}}{4} -\\dfrac{x^{-1}}{\\left(-1\\right)} +C \\\\[5pt]\n\n&= -\\dfrac  {3}{\\sqrt[3]{x}} + \\dfrac{x^4}{4} + \\dfrac{1}{x} +C.\n\n\n}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":3769,"name":"The Sum Rule for Indefinite Integrals"},"example":{"id":373,"title":"Integrating Sums of Power Functions"},"group":{"id":97345,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14249144,"answer":{"id":62298158,"cread":"2026-10-15T19:31:27.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14103},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]}],"localGraph":{"topicId":3769,"topics":[{"id":43,"name":"The Constant Multiple Rule for Indefinite Integrals","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":1.3555685233612444,"repetition":2,"stability":0.1810777490859353},{"id":285,"name":"Integrating Trigonometric Functions","prerequisites":[3769]},{"id":304,"name":"Integrating Hyperbolic Functions","prerequisites":[3769]},{"id":334,"name":"Integrating Algebraic Functions Using Substitution","prerequisites":[3769],"frontier":1,"halfLife":0.1,"repetition":0,"stability":0},{"id":342,"name":"Integration Using Inverse Trigonometric Functions","prerequisites":[3769]},{"id":1361,"name":"Integrating the Reciprocal Function","prerequisites":[3769],"frontier":1,"halfLife":0.1,"repetition":0,"stability":0},{"id":3769,"name":"The Sum Rule for Indefinite Integrals","prerequisites":[43],"fr